### Footnotes
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">

Footnotes are plain Markdown (`pymdownx` / `footnotes` extension): drop a `[^ref]`
marker in the prose and define it anywhere on the page.  They collect at the
bottom and back-link automatically.

A reference marker renders as a superscript link[^demo], and several markers can
share a page[^second]; ordering of the *definitions* does not matter.

```markdown
A reference marker renders as a superscript link[^demo].

[^demo]: The definition can live anywhere on the page.
```

[^demo]: The definition can live anywhere on the page; python-markdown gathers them into the footnote list and wires the back-link.
[^second]: A second footnote, to show the numbering and back-links stack.
